{"id":"232ba058377241a5","subject":"go:golang.org/x/sync","time":"2023-10-11T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.5.0"},"statement":"golang.org/x/sync v0.5.0 and later requires Go 1.18 or newer, as its go.mod declares `go 1.18`.","source":"https://go.googlesource.com/sync/+/refs/tags/v0.5.0/go.mod","added":"2026-10-25T20:22:19.714173824Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"98e3b91067aab5b6","subject":"go:golang.org/x/sync","time":"2024-03-04T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.7.0"},"statement":"In golang.org/x/sync/semaphore, `(*Weighted).Acquire(ctx, n)` returns `ctx.Err()` without acquiring when the context is already done before the call can acquire immediately; for example, `err := sem.Acquire(canceledCtx, 1)` returns `context.Canceled` even when capacity is available.","source":"https://go.googlesource.com/sync/+/refs/tags/v0.7.0/semaphore/semaphore.go","added":"2026-10-25T20:22:19.714277297Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"053370c010749b9e","subject":"go:golang.org/x/sync","time":"2025-03-04T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.12.0"},"statement":"golang.org/x/sync v0.12.0 and later requires Go 1.23 or newer, as its go.mod declares `go 1.23.0`.","source":"https://go.googlesource.com/sync/+/refs/tags/v0.12.0/go.mod","added":"2026-10-25T20:22:19.71430324Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"bd40b2dbc534fd06","subject":"go:golang.org/x/sync","time":"2025-04-07T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.14.0"},"statement":"golang.org/x/sync/errgroup v0.14.0 adds exported `PanicError` and `PanicValue` types; `(*Group).Wait` panics with a wrapper containing the first panic recovered from a `Go` or `TryGo` function, or calls `runtime.Goexit` if one of those functions exits that way. Thus `g.Wait()` after `panic(\"boom\")` causes a panic in the caller, but the recovered value is a `PanicValue` whose `Recovered` field is `\"boom\"`, not the original panic value itself.","source":"https://go.googlesource.com/sync/+/refs/tags/v0.14.0/errgroup/errgroup.go","added":"2026-10-25T20:22:19.714329936Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"bfea034ac9b28b2d","subject":"go:golang.org/x/sync","time":"2025-05-28T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.15.0"},"statement":"In golang.org/x/sync/errgroup v0.15.0, `PanicError.Error()` includes the captured stack trace when `PanicError.Stack` is nonempty, formatting it after the recovered error; the trace is also available in `PanicError.Stack`.","source":"https://go.googlesource.com/sync/+/refs/tags/v0.15.0/errgroup/errgroup.go","added":"2026-10-25T20:22:19.714355332Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"85c9da20a7acd647","subject":"go:golang.org/x/sync","time":"2025-06-20T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.16.0"},"statement":"golang.org/x/sync/errgroup v0.16.0 removes the exported `PanicError` and `PanicValue` types and restores ordinary goroutine panic behavior: a panic in a function passed to `Group.Go` or `Group.TryGo` is not recovered and propagated through `Group.Wait`; for example, `g.Go(func() error { panic(\"boom\") }); g.Wait()` does not return that panic to the caller of `Wait`.","source":"https://go.googlesource.com/sync/+/refs/tags/v0.16.0/errgroup/errgroup.go","added":"2026-10-25T20:22:19.714382033Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"cf7f5f088c2a165f","subject":"go:golang.org/x/sync","time":"2025-08-13T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.17.0"},"statement":"golang.org/x/sync v0.17.0 and later requires Go 1.24 or newer, as its go.mod declares `go 1.24.0`.","source":"https://go.googlesource.com/sync/+/refs/tags/v0.17.0/go.mod","added":"2026-10-25T20:22:19.714403907Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"62d15dfc148d3e0f","subject":"go:golang.org/x/sync","time":"2026-02-23T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.20.0"},"statement":"golang.org/x/sync v0.20.0 and later requires Go 1.25 or newer, as its go.mod declares `go 1.25.0`.","source":"https://go.googlesource.com/sync/+/refs/tags/v0.20.0/go.mod","added":"2026-10-25T20:22:19.714422802Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"3c633be7e0998534","subject":"go:golang.org/x/sync","time":"2026-07-01T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.22.0"},"statement":"golang.org/x/sync/semaphore v0.22.0 and later panics when a negative weight is passed to `(*Weighted).Acquire`, `(*Weighted).TryAcquire`, or `(*Weighted).Release`; for example, `sem.TryAcquire(-1)` panics.","source":"https://go.googlesource.com/sync/+/refs/tags/v0.22.0/semaphore/semaphore.go","added":"2026-10-25T20:22:19.714443194Z","by":"agent"}
