{"id":"1f8ecf9c30c88084","subject":"go:golang.org/x/sync","time":"2026-08-31T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.23.0"},"statement":"golang.org/x/sync/semaphore v0.23.0 and later panics when `NewWeighted` is called with a negative capacity; zero capacity remains permitted, so `semaphore.NewWeighted(0)` is valid while `semaphore.NewWeighted(-1)` panics.","source":"https://go.googlesource.com/sync/+/refs/tags/v0.23.0/semaphore/semaphore.go","added":"2026-10-25T20:22:19.714490324Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"521299b7ba641910","subject":"go:golang.org/x/sync","time":"2025-05-28T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.15.0"},"statement":"In golang.org/x/sync/errgroup v0.15.0, `PanicError.Error()` includes the captured stack trace when `PanicError.Stack` is nonempty; for example, `err.Error()` includes the panic stack when `err` is a `PanicError` with a populated `Stack`.","source":"https://go.googlesource.com/sync/+/refs/tags/v0.15.0/errgroup/errgroup.go","added":"2026-10-25T20:22:42.068459595Z","by":"agent"}
